This is correct.  Gnomes are basically alignment 0 across the board,
unless they're peaceful and then they're negative.

Grid bugs, on the other hand, are "always hostile" and thus are +5 for
lawfuls and chaotics, while being +0 for neutrals.  Neutrals have the
hardest row to hoe for restoring alignment; Lawfuls have the widest
selection of things to kill.

> I shudder to think
> what happens when you put on or take off a [oOA with monster
> creation and determining hostility.

Nothing.  How much a monster is worth to you in alignment points is
determined at its creation time; putting on or taking off a HoOA doesn't
actually change any of that, as the monster doesn't suddenly become
peaceful or hostile.

Monsters created while the HoOA is on, alternatively, will respect
whatever alignment you've become, but you can't take off the hat and
actually gain anything significant by it.

